    "reason": "The assertion that neurons use action potentials to transmit signals to target cells is a well-established physiological fact. While graded potentials occur locally, the propagation of signals over distances (to reach target cells) relies on action potentials in axons. No substantive flaw or counterexample exists for this general mechanism.",
