    "reason": "The assertion that dendrites receive incoming signals at synapses from other neurons or glial cells is factually accurate. Synapses are the primary sites of signal reception on dendrites (and sometimes cell bodies), and inputs originate from axon terminals of other neurons or, less commonly, from glial cells. No counterexample refutes this standard biological description.",
    "sound_as_stated": true,
    "counterexample": null
  }
